{
  "id": "boundary-issues",
  "term": "boundary issues",
  "definition": "In cognition, boundary issues are the problem of deciding what counts as the actual conscious system when a measure of consciousness also seems to apply to its parts, to larger irrelevant extensions, or to groups made up of conscious individuals. The term refers to uncertainty about where the boundaries of consciousness should be drawn and whether the measured properties truly belong to the system itself.",
